tions across the Americas is often dismissed in Spain as the \\\"Leyenda Negra\\\" (Black Legend)—an Anglo-Protestant propaganda myth designed to make the Spanish Catholic empire look exceptionally cruel. As a result, many Spaniards defend their colonial legacy as cultural synthesis rather than violent exploitation.\",[[0,6,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[104,119,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Why the Amnesia Persists\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Defensive Nationalism: Admitting that your modern wealth, grand museums, and global stature were financed by looting, deindustrializing, and enslaving other continents directly threatens the national self-image of being enlightened champions of democracy and human rights.\",[[0,22,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Curriculum Decentralization: In countries like the UK, exam boards and individual headteachers choose specific history modules. Teachers frequently pick WWI and WWII because resources are plentiful and the narrative is unambiguous: the nation fought on the side of moral good.\",[[0,28,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Political Culture Wars: Whenever progressive educators or historians push for decolonizing history curricula, right-wing political parties and tabloid media attack them for \\\"teaching self-hatred\\\" or \\\"guilt-tripping children.\\\"\",[[0,23,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]],1]],[null,[null,0,\"While younger generations in Europe are reading more about colonialism through university courses, grassroots activism, and social media, the average European citizen still walks down streets named after colonial governors with little idea of what was done to build their cities.\"]]]]],null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",null,null,1,1],[1789201915,868969000]],[[\"c_e87b6c6ac16404a5\",\"r_333a9df53520b835\"],[\"c_e87b6c6ac16404a5\",\"r_510473f4292874f2\",\"rc_40125598534228a6\"],[[\"Wow, so RSS is achieving is objective in homogenizing India.  \",null,null,null,[[]]],2,null,1,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,null,false,null,[]],[[[\"rc_939b6b1f0f34805b\",[\"While it looks like a clean sweep on paper, what is actually happening is institutional coercion rather than true cultural or linguistic assimilation. \\n\\nThe Centre has accumulated structural leverage over education, but attempting to homogenize a civilization as polycentric as India comes with steep costs and hard limits.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Where the Hegemonic Project Is Working\\n\\n* **Fiscal Arm-Twisting:** The Centre tied critical welfare and infrastructure funding—like the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and PM SHRI model schools—directly to states adopting the NEP. States struggling with revenue deficits (such as Kerala) were eventually pressured into signing MoUs just to unlock thousands of crores in withheld educational funds.\\n* **Control of Central Boards:** CBSE, ICSE, Navodaya Vidyalayas, and Kendriya Vidyalayas serve the mobile middle class, civil servants, and military families across every state. By enforcing NEP norms in these systems, the Union government bypasses state education ministries entirely, normalizing Hindi and Sanskrit among urban youth in non-Hindi capitals.\\n* **National Competitive Exams:** Key national entrance gates (NEET, CUET, SSC, UPSC, and central banking exams) remain structurally tilted toward English and Hindi. Even when regional language options are added, question phrasing, source material, and answer keys are overwhelmingly developed in Hindi or English, forcing ambitious students nationwide to build literacy in those two tongues.\\n* **Asymmetric Hindi Spending:** Budgets for the promotion of Hindi and Sanskrit dwarf allocations for classical languages like Tamil, Telugu, Kannada, or Malayalam by orders of magnitude, effectively subsidizing the infrastructure of northern linguistic spread.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Why the Project Hits a Wall\\n\\nDespite that institutional muscle, equating policy decrees with actual homogenization ignores several critical counter-currents:\\n\\n* **Tamil Nadu’s Iron Wall:** Tamil Nadu remains the structural barrier to total uniformity. Across party lines—from DMK to AIADMK and new regional outfits—the state strictly enforces its 1968 two-language policy. The state has forfeited thousands of crores in central grants and challenged fund withholdings in the Supreme Court rather than capitulate to the three-language mandate. \\n* **Classroom vs. Street Reality:** Passing a third-language Hindi exam to meet board criteria in Karnataka, Telangana, or Maharashtra rarely translates to social adoption. Students memorize enough to clear the board requirement, then discard it in favor of their mother tongue locally and English globally. Formal compliance does not equal cultural assimilation.\\n* **Linguistic Re-Assertion in Other Southern States:** Pushback is no longer isolated to Tamil Nadu. In Karnataka, agitations by Kannada groups over bank signage, central exams, and metropolitan service desks have intensified. The language question has increasingly turned into a flashpoint over local jobs and demographic shifts caused by inter-state migration.\\n* **The Looming Delimitation Shock:** The deeper friction point isn't just school textbooks—it’s parliamentary representation. If parliamentary seats are redrawn based on raw population, the northern states (which lagged in family planning) stand to gain massive legislative power over the southern states (which successfully controlled population growth and generate disproportionate tax revenue). Language imposition acts as the cultural canary in the coal mine for this broader federal crisis.\\n\\nThe RSS and the central apparatus can use administrative carrots and sticks to mandate languages on school report cards. However, turning a federation of historically rooted linguistic nationalities into a unified, monolingual cultural bloc faces deep organic resistance.\\n\\nA grounded analysis of how this policy plays out on the ground can be seen in the explainer [Is the three language formula actually working?](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\\u003dvPTY8pRAPkA).\\n\\nThis report examines whether the Three-Language Formula is actually fulfilling its stated educational goals or merely deepening federal and regional fault lines.\\nhttp://googleusercontent.com/youtube_content/1\"],[null,[[[\"The Centre tied critical welfare and infrastructure funding—like the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and PM SHRI model schools—directly to states adopting the NEP.\",null,null,[[401,566],[401,562]]],[1],[[\"https://sabrangindia.in/tamil-nadus-opposition-to-nep-2020s-three-language-formula-a-federal-pushback-against-central-imposition/#:~:text\\u003dDespite%20this%20intended%20flexibility%2C%20Tamil%20Nadu%20remains,For%20Tamil%20Nadu%2C%20this%20conditionality%20is%20unacceptable%3B\",\"Tamil Nadu's opposition to NEP 2020's three-language formula\",\"https://encrypted-tbn1.gstatic.com/favicon-tbn?q\\u003dtbn%3AANd9GcQ3mBsAA9ooZlLBcUIWKVNRBpuRGrQNXMTFBWszZjrimlXO-KbI1NIpTlKCoa6LGpkxg5-gOQoaDx2pIiNriwS6gEVobDdn81eN9w\",\"Despite this intended flexibility, Tamil Nadu remains deeply sceptical. The \\nstate interprets the policy as a thinly veiled effort to introduce Hindi \\ninto its sc...\",[[\"The Centre tied critical welfare and infrastructure funding—like the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and PM SHRI model schools—directly to states adopting the NEP.\",null,null,[[401,566],[401,562]]]],null,\"Sabrang India\",9,\"\"]],\"spp_6dca05b42ed54bff\"],[[\"States struggling with revenue deficits (such as Kerala) were eventually pressured into signing MoUs just to unlock thousands of crores in withheld educational funds.\",null,null,[[567,733],[563,729]]],[1],[[\"https://thesouthfirst.com/telangana/done-telangan