rching the web\"],4]]],[[null,[\"google\",[null,null,\"Google Search\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/images/branding/productlogos/googleg/v6/192px.svg\",null,\"Searching the web\"],4]]],null,null,\"IN\",true,null,null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"The push for the three-language formula through policies like the National Education Policy (NEP) exposes the fundamental tension between a centralized, homogenization-driven nation-state project and India’s reality as a multilingual, multinational federation.\",[[140,195,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[221,259,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[0,260,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_cc34e5efaaef4786\"]]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"To the Sangh Parivar, linguistic taxonomy (Indo-Aryan vs. Dravidian) is secondary to an ideological vision: constructing a singular, cohesive national identity.\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"1. The Ideological Blueprint: \\\"Hindi, Hindu, Hindustan\\\"\"]],[null,[null,0,\"The RSS’s foundational philosophy, derived from early ideologues like V.D. Savarkar and M.S. Golwalkar, views national strength through the European-derived 19th-century lens of cultural homogeneity: one people, one culture, one language.\",[[200,237,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"A Bridge to Sanskrit: In the Hindutva framework, Sanskrit is the sacred civilizational core (Devabhasha). Standard Hindi (written in Devanagari and heavily Sanskritized) is treated as the modern, demographically viable proxy to unify the country under a Sanskritic cultural umbrella.\",[[0,21,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[93,103,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The \\\"Link Language\\\" Argument: As articulated repeatedly by political leaders like Amit Shah, the BJP’s policy posture is that India needs an indigenous lingua franca rather than relying on English, which they frame as a colonial relic. Because Hindi has the largest demographic footprint in northern and central India, it is treated as the default national conduit.\",[[0,29,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[152,165,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[30,235,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_596ad1e3011548e6\"]]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"2. How the NEP Formula Functions as Backdoor Imposition\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Officially, the NEP text emphasizes \\\"multilingual flexibility\\\" and states that no specific language will be imposed, mandating only that two of the three languages be native Indian languages. However, critics and state governments (notably Tamil Nadu) argue that in practice, the structural mechanics ensure Hindi becomes mandatory:\",[[0,191,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_86b1d99fb65492b\"]]]],[192,332,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_bdb71a8760d14db5\"]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The Two-Indian-Language Mandate: Most non-Hindi states run on a two-language system: the state language + English. By requiring students to pick two native Indian languages plus an optional third (usually English), schools are compelled to find another Indian language.\",[[0,32,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[33,114,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_a55f823b2bba49f5\"]]]],[115,269,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_904d0f8570c94b4f\"]]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Resource Asymmetry: The Union government heavily subsidizes Hindi education (funding Hindi teachers, Hindi prachar sabhas, and central textbooks). A school in Madurai or Tiruchirappalli cannot easily hire teachers for Bengali, Odia, or Marathi. The only Indian language with readily available teachers, materials, and central funding is Hindi. The \\\"choice\\\" becomes an illusion.\",[[0,19,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[20,146,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_10a9e4b7be5d49ce\"]]]],[344,377,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_b0387b4fade44242\"]]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Failure of Reciprocity: The original 1968 Three-Language Formula mandated that northern states teach a South Indian language alongside Hindi and English. Instead, northern states almost universally adopted Sanskrit or Urdu as their \\\"third language,\\\" completely ignoring southern Dravidian tongues. The burden of learning an additional living language fell entirely onto non-Hindi speakers.\",[[0,23,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[24,153,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_256d5f6700f640e6\"]]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Fiscal Coercion: The Centre has repeatedly conditioned federal educational funds (such as the Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan) on states adopting the NEP framework. Non-compliant states face funding cuts, turning language adoption into an ultimatum.\",[[0,16,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[94,117,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[17,156,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_236a9fa3a90a4f47\"]]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"3. Why Linguistics Doesn't Factor into Their Calculations\"]],[null,[null,0,\"From a cladistic and historical linguistic standpoint, pushing an Indo-Aryan (Indo-European) language onto Dravidian-speaking populations makes no natural sense. The language families have distinct phonologies, grammars, roots, and evolutionary paths.\"]],[null,[null,0,\"However, the RSS rejects this linguistic separation:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Denial of the Aryan-Dravidian Division: Hindutva historiography rejects the Indo-Aryan migration model and downplays Caldwell’s classification of Dravidian languages as an entirely distinct family.\",[[0,39,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The \\\"All Languages Evolved from Sanskrit\\\" Myth: RSS-affiliated educational bodies consistently advance the claim that all Indian languages (including Tamil, Kannada, and Telugu) are derived from or heavily indebted to Sanskrit. Under this belief system, spreading Hindi or Sanskritized vocabulary to the South is not seen as foreign displacement, but as restoring a civilizational continuum.\",[[0,47,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"4. The Political \\u0026 Economic Stakes for the South\"]],[null,[null,0,\"For states like Tamil Nadu, rejecting the three-language formula is not just about phonetics—it is about asymmetric disadvantage and federal autonomy:\",[[105,149,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[0,150,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_7d940342b814b7a\"]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Dimension\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The South's Reality (Two-Language System)\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The Centralized Imposition Model\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Cognitive Load\",[[0,14,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Students master the local mother tongue (Tamil) and the global link language (English).\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Non-Hindi students must learn three languages, while native Hindi students effectively learn two (Hindi + English).\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Employment\",[[0,10,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"English provides access to the global knowledge economy, IT, and international trade.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Hindi provides zero distinct economic advantage outside regional northern markets.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Public Sector Exams\",[[0,19,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Southern aspirants face a structural handicap in Union civil services and banking exams where Hindi is heavily prioritized.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Native Hindi speakers gain an unfair competitive advantage in federal governance jobs.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,[null,0,\"By using the NEP to embed Hindi nationwide, the BJP and RSS are attempting to build an administrative and cultural monoculture that eases political centralisation from Delhi. For non-Hindi states, defending the two-language policy is the primary defensive barrier preserving linguistic self-determination and genuine federalism.\",[[175,328,[null,null,null,[null,[\"spp_c0230f7f80f14304\"]]]]]]]]]],null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",null,null,1,1],[1789201870,156963000]],[[\"c_e87b6c6ac16404a5\",\"r_12890d546c20aba3\"],[\"c_e87b6c6ac16404a5\",\"r_d657e5904ea69496\",\"rc_f50f63bc151d32d8\"],[[\"Why does the RSS claim that they are indigenous to India, when the mainstream historical and genetic evidence supports Indo-Aryan migration into the subcontinent? And why do some Tamil nationalists describe RSS gang as vantheris? \",null,null,null,[[]]],2,null,1,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,null,false,null,[]],[[[\"rc_8a7f115f22a0479b\",[\"Both claims stem from the ideological need to define **who belongs and who is an outsider**, using deep history and genetics as battlegrounds to legitimize political authority.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Why the RSS Claims \\\"Indigenous Aryans\\\" (OIT)\\n\\nMainstream population genetics (such as ancient DNA studies led by Vagheesh Narasimhan, David Reich, et al.) and historical linguistics show that the Indian gene pool is primarily a mixture of Ancestral South Indian (ASI) and Ancestral North Indian (ANI) lineages, with the Steppe pastoralist (Indo-Aryan) ancestry arriving roughly between 2000 BCE and 1500 BCE.\\n\\nDespite this consensus, the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS) and Hindu nationalist historiography reject the Indo-Aryan Migration theory—often backing the \\\"Out of India\\\" theory (OIT) or \\\"Indigenous Aryans\\\" narrative—for clear ideological reasons:\\n\\n* **Defining the \\\"Punya-bhumi\\\" (Holy Land):** In V.D. Savarkar’s formulation of *Hindutva*, a Hindu is someone who considers the subcontinent both their *Pitr-bhumi* (fatherland/ancestral land) and *Punya-bhumi* (holy land). If Vedic culture and the Indo-Aryans originated outside the subcontinent, it undermines the moral high ground used against Muslims and Christians, whose religions originated outside India.\\n* **Neutralizing the \\\"Invader\\\" Analogy:** A core political thesis of the RSS is that India’s civilizational decline was caused by successive waves of \\\"foreign invaders\\\" (primarily Turkic/Mughal and British). If Aryans were also migrants who brought Vedic religion, Sanskrit, and early caste hierarchies from Central Asia, the distinction between \\\"native\\\" and \\\"foreign\\\" collapses.\\n* **Colonial Trauma and Aryan Supremacist Theories:** The 19th-century British \\\"Aryan Invasion Theory\\\" was used by colonial administrators to divide Indians and justify British rule (arguing that civilized rule had always come from lighter-skinned outsiders). In reacting against this colonial framework, the RSS pivoted to the opposite extreme: asserting that Vedic civilization was 100% indigenous and that Sanskrit-speaking peoples migrated *outward* to civilize the rest of Eurasia.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Why Tamil Nationalists Use the Term *Vantheris*\\n\\n*Vantheri* (வந்தேறி) is a Tamil compound word meaning \\\"one who came and settled\\\" (an outsider, immigrant, or usurper). In Tamil nationalist and Dravidian political rhetoric, the RSS, the broader Sangh Parivar, and North Indian-centric political groups are frequently labeled *vantheris* for distinct historical and linguistic reasons:\\n\\n* **The Dravidian vs. Aryan Dichotomy:** Rooted in the non-Brahmin movement, Periyar’s Self-Respect Movement, and the linguistic discoveries of Robert Caldwell in the 19th century, Dravidian and Tamil nationalist ideology posits that Dravidian speakers were the original, indigenous inhabitants of the subcontinent (often linking them to the Indus Valley Civilization). In this framing, Vedic culture, the varna/caste hierarchy, and Sanskrit are treated as external, intrusive systems brought by northern migrants.\\n* **Anti-Brahminism and Northern Hegemony:** Because the RSS’s ideological origins are deeply rooted in Chitpavan and Maharashtrian Brahmin leadership, and because its cultural program heavily emphasizes Hindi, Sanskrit, and pan-Indian Vedic ritualism, Tamil nationalists view the RSS as an instrument of Northern/Aryan socio-political dominance attempting to displace native Tamil identity and autonomy.\\n* **Weaponizing Nativism:** Just as the RSS uses the concept of \\\"foreignness\\\" against religious minorities, Tamil nationalists (particularly hardline factions like Seeman’s Naam Tamilar Katchi) use the *vantheri* label to create an internal/external boundary. Anyone seen as representing pan-Indian centralism, northern economic migration, or Sanskritic cultural hegemony is categorized as an interloper trying to rule over native Tamils.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### The Underlying Parallel\\n\\nBoth arguments rely on **nativism as political legitimacy**:\\n\\n| Ideological Camp | Narrative of \\\"Native\\\" | The \\\"Outsider\\\" (*Vantheri* / Invader) |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| **RSS / Hindutva** | Vedic/Aryan culture is completely indigenous to the subcontinent. | Abrahamic religions, Islamic rule, Westernization, and theories of external migration. |\\n| **Tamil Nationalists** | Dravidian/Tamil linguistic identity is the true indigenous root of the land. | Northern hegemony, Sanskritic/Vedic ideology, Hindi imposition, and the RSS. |\\n\\nBoth positions weaponize prehistoric migrations to fight 21st-century battles over political power, language rights, and state authority.\"],null,null,null,null,null,null,[2],\"en\",null,null,[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]]],null,null,\"rc_8a7f115f22a0479b\",null,null,null,null,\"IN\",true,null,null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Both claims stem from the ideological need to define who belongs and who is an outsider, using deep history and genetics as battlegrounds to legitimize political authority.\",[[53,87,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Why the RSS Claims \\\"Indigenous Aryans\\\" (OIT)\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Mainstream population genetics (such as ancient DNA studies led by Vagheesh Narasimhan, David Reich, et al.) and historical linguistics show that the Indian gene pool is primarily a mixture of Ancestral South Indian (ASI) and Ancestral North Indian (ANI) lineages, with the Steppe pastoralist (Indo-Aryan) ancestry arriving roughly between 2000 BCE and 1500 BCE.\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Despite this consensus, the Rashtriya Swayamsevak Sangh (RSS) and Hindu nationalist historiography reject the Indo-Aryan Migration theory—often backing the \\\"Out of India\\\" theory (OIT) or \\\"Indigenous Aryans\\\" narrative—for clear ideological reasons:\"]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"Defining the \\\"Punya-bhumi\\\" (Holy Land): In V.D. Savarkar’s formulation of Hindutva, a Hindu is someone who considers the subcontinent both their Pitr-bhumi (fatherland/ancestral land) and Punya-bhumi (holy land). If Vedic culture and the Indo-Aryans originated outside the subcontinent, it undermines the moral high ground used against Muslims and Christians, whose religions originated outside India.\",[[0,39,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[74,82,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[145,155,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[188,199,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Neutralizing the \\\"Invader\\\" Analogy: A core political thesis of the RSS is that India’s civilizational decline was caused by successive waves of \\\"foreign invaders\\\" (primarily Turkic/Mughal and British). If Aryans were also migrants who brought Vedic religion, Sanskrit, and early caste hierarchies from Central Asia, the distinction between \\\"native\\\" and \\\"foreign\\\" collapses.\",[[0,35,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Colonial Trauma and Aryan Supremacist Theories: The 19th-century British \\\"Aryan Invasion Theory\\\" was used by colonial administrators to divide Indians and justify British rule (arguing that civilized rule had always come from lighter-skinned outsiders). In reacting against this colonial framework, the RSS pivoted to the opposite extreme: asserting that Vedic civilization was 100% indigenous and that Sanskrit-speaking peoples migrated outward to civilize the rest of Eurasia.\",[[0,47,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[438,445,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"Why Tamil Nationalists Use the Term Vantheris\",[[36,45,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]],[null,[null,0,\"Vantheri (வந்தேறி) is a Tamil compound word meaning \\\"one who came and settled\\\" (an outsider, immigrant, or usurper). In Tamil nationalist and Dravidian political rhetoric, the RSS, the broader Sangh Parivar, and North Indian-centric political groups are frequently labeled vantheris for distinct historical and linguistic reasons:\",[[0,8,[[null,null,null,null,1]]],[273,282,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[[[null,[null,0,\"The Dravidian vs. Aryan Dichotomy: Rooted in the non-Brahmin movement, Periyar’s Self-Respect Movement, and the linguistic discoveries of Robert Caldwell in the 19th century, Dravidian and Tamil nationalist ideology posits that Dravidian speakers were the original, indigenous inhabitants of the subcontinent (often linking them to the Indus Valley Civilization). In this framing, Vedic culture, the varna/caste hierarchy, and Sanskrit are treated as external, intrusive systems brought by northern migrants.\",[[0,34,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Anti-Brahminism and Northern Hegemony: Because the RSS’s ideological origins are deeply rooted in Chitpavan and Maharashtrian Brahmin leadership, and because its cultural program heavily emphasizes Hindi, Sanskrit, and pan-Indian Vedic ritualism, Tamil nationalists view the RSS as an instrument of Northern/Aryan socio-political dominance attempting to displace native Tamil identity and autonomy.\",[[0,38,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Weaponizing Nativism: Just as the RSS uses the concept of \\\"foreignness\\\" against religious minorities, Tamil nationalists (particularly hardline factions like Seeman’s Naam Tamilar Katchi) use the vantheri label to create an internal/external boundary. Anyone seen as representing pan-Indian centralism, northern economic migration, or Sanskritic cultural hegemony is categorized as an interloper trying to rule over native Tamils.\",[[0,21,[[null,null,null,null,2]]],[196,204,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[]],[null,[null,3,\"The Underlying Parallel\"]],[null,[null,0,\"Both arguments rely on nativism as political legitimacy:\",[[23,55,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]],[null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,[[[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Ideological Camp\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Narrative of \\\"Native\\\"\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"The \\\"Outsider\\\" (Vantheri / Invader)\",[[16,24,[[null,null,null,null,1]]]]]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"RSS / Hindutva\",[[0,14,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Vedic/Aryan culture is completely indigenous to the subcontinent.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Abrahamic religions, Islamic rule, Westernization, and theories of external migration.\"]]]]]],[null,[[[[null,[null,0,\"Tamil Nationalists\",[[0,18,[[null,null,null,null,2]]]]]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Dravidian/Tamil linguistic identity is the true indigenous root of the land.\"]]]],[[[null,[null,0,\"Northern hegemony, Sanskritic/Vedic ideology, Hindi imposition, and the RSS.\"]]]]]]],true]],[null,[null,0,\"Both positions weaponize prehistoric migrations to fight 21st-century battles over political power, language rights, and state authority.\"]]]]],null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,\"56fdd199312815e2\",null,null,null,\"3.8 Flash\",null,null,1,1],[1789201845,468455000]]],\"\",null,[]]",null,null,null,"generic"]]
